# Failure / stuck-loop learning

Learning specialization of the always-on Harness. On failure, run this protocol inside the loop.

## Triggers (same turn)

- Acceptance fails / task failure / stuck loop
- Owner must repeat an instruction
- Owner disputes a reported result
- Owner voids prior guidance (“forget…”, “update your memory”)

## Protocol

1. Stop the bad loop (no re-defense of the failed report).
2. Diagnose with evidence.
3. Append `docs/memory/learnings.md` — VOID superseded entries when guidance changes.
4. **Harden the class** (rule + craft + mechanical gate) — not only the one instance.
5. Re-test / re-issue under the new playbook.
6. Escalate last (A/B/C if two SoTs disagree).

## Learn the class

Instance patch alone is incomplete. Ask: what family of mistakes is this? Encode a rule that blocks the family (e.g. all internal sensors off owner-facing tables — not “omit this one column”).

## Owner-facing

Owner Match?/dry-run/verify = owner SoT + Amount in system only. Gate: `src/lib/owner-facing-report.ts`. Craft: `docs/craft/owner-facing-sensors.md` + `docs/craft/failure-stuck-loop-learning.md`.
